# MSA letter zoom column fills

When editing Overview MSA letter rendering (`_msa_letter_bg_rect`,
`zoom_bounds`, letter paint paths):

## Zoom behaviour

| Slider | Fill |
|--------|------|
| ~¾ (size-10) | Square residue background |
| ¾ → max | Width follows the column pitch; height stays size-10 |
| Max | Columns are **flush** — no white gutters between neighbouring letters |

## Required

- Past the square stage, letter backgrounds must span the **full** column
  width (`cell_w`), not a capped inset that leaves gaps at max zoom.
- MSA max zoom should target about **3×** the size-10 `ppb`
  (`_MSA_LETTER_BG_MAX_WIDTH_SCALE`), not a larger over-fit ceiling that
  reintroduces gutters.
- Helpers live in `multi_sequence_overview.py`: `_msa_letter_bg_rect`,
  `_msa_letter_size_metrics`, `_MSA_LETTER_*` constants.

## Do not

- Cap fill width below `cell_w` once past size-10 (that creates the white
  column gaps at max zoom).
- “Fix” max zoom by only raising `_MSA_MAX_PPB` without keeping fills
  flush to the column pitch.
